e. The F01 to F05 hint templates are true statements about circles, rectangles, squares and triangles, and sides_label is always sides through the vocabulary gate. No printed value uses a NOT_YET_KNOWN term. Every question is under 18 words per sentence and uses plain numerals. Not a Rule 1 failure, but noted: the printed forms half-circle and quarter-circle are hyphenated, while the lc text and curriculum_vocab read half circle and quarter circle. F02 mentions that opposite sides of a rectangle are equal. This is true and uses no gated vocabulary, though it describes a shape outside the lc's named objects.\"}",
